I form B5-B6-B7 (Chow), then maybe W6-W7-W8? No W8. T2 could be part of a Pung if I have two more. No. T6 is single. T9 is single. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can have a pair of T6? No, only one. \n\nHmm. It seems like even after Peng T8, the hand isn't complete. So Peng T8 isn't helpful. Therefore, the best action is to pass.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The available action is to Peng T8, but forming this Pung does not lead to a complete or high-scoring hand. The remaining tiles lack sufficient melds to form a winning combination.  \nReason: Peng T8 would create a Pung of T8s, but the remaining tiles (W6, W7, T2, T6, T9, B5, B6, B7, B9, F3, J2) cannot form three additional valid melds and a pair. The hand remains incomplete, and passing avoids committing to a suboptimal move.  \nAnswer: Pass"}
