 that might form melds.\\n\\nAlternatively, discarding B5 might be risky because it's adjacent to B6 in the meld. So if the user discards B5, someone might take it for a Chow with B4 or B6.\\n\\nTherefore, the best option is to discard J2.\\n\", \"output\": \"Evaluation: [Discard J2 to eliminate an unused tile and avoid giving others a chance to complete a meld with it.]\\nReason: [J2 is a single tile with no potential for forming a meld or pair in the current hand. Discarding it removes a liability and preserves other tiles that could contribute to completing the hand. Other tiles like T8 (a pair) or W6 (potential for a pung) are more valuable to retain.]\\nAnswer: Play J2\"}"}
